<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ine of Wessex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 670–c. 728</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> was king of the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> from 688 to 726, one of the strongest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> rulers before Alfred. He issued an important law code, founded or endowed churches including Glastonbury, and pushed West Saxon power westward into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerset">Somerset</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devon">Devon</a>, fighting King Geraint of the British kingdom of Dumnonia around 710. He abdicated in 726 and went on pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ine-of-wessex.jpg" alt="Ine of Wessex" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Greenshed · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Ine_in_the_Transfiguration_Window_of_Wells_Cathedral_(crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Ine</b>’s laws give Britons lower wergilds than Englishmen, showing that a large British population lived under West Saxon rule.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-wessex">Kingdom of Wessex · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Its kings are poorly recorded; Geraint fought <b>Ine of Wessex</b> around 710.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-cornwall">Kingdom of Cornwall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 710 <b>Ine of Wessex</b> fought Geraint, and Devon was gradually absorbed.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-dumnonia">Kingdom of Dumnonia</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.89,12.48&amp;year=707" aria-label="Rome on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4854 672 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Ine of Wessex"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5304 942h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=41.89,12.48&amp;year=707">What was here in 707 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
